# L4 Scoring Model Rules

Source: *Soccermatics* [SM], *Algorithmic Trading* [Chan]. See
`docs/QUANT_ARCHITECTURE.md` Part I.

- **Generative over exact scores.** The model MUST produce a bivariate
  Poisson / Dixon-Coles **score matrix**. Derive 1X2, totals, double-chance and
  tournament markets by COLLAPSING that matrix — never model them as independent
  heads [SM].
- **Simplicity & linearity.** Keep parameters minimal; the rate link MUST be
  log-linear (`log λ = c + home + attack_i + defence_j`); regularise team
  strengths. Added nonlinearity/free parameters invite data-snooping bias and
  require explicit justification [Chan].
- **World Cup structure.** Model group stage (draws allowed) and knockouts (no
  draw; extra time / penalties) distinctly. Do not reuse raw group-stage draw
  mass for knockout markets [SM].
- **Recency.** Weight fixtures with time decay; never treat a 1950 and a 2025
  international as equally informative.
- **Interface parity.** Every model MUST expose `fit` / `predict` /
  `match_probabilities(home, away, neutral=...)` returning
  `{"home","draw","away"}`, plus `model_version` and `knows_team()`, so it stays
  a drop-in for the pipeline.

```python
# ✅ derive every market from the one score matrix
m = model.score_matrix(home, away, neutral=True)
one_x_two = model.matrix_to_1x2(m)   # not three separate fitted models
```
